# Uniflex — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (same folder) and fill in real values there.
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed — this file (.env.example)
# is the only one that should ever be tracked in git, and it must only ever
# hold placeholder names, never real keys or secrets.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A KEY
#
# `.env` is listed under `assets:` in pubspec.yaml, which means Flutter
# bundles it *verbatim* into the built APK/IPA. Anyone can unzip a release
# build and read it. So `.env` may only ever contain values that are safe
# to hand to an attacker:
#
#   • Supabase URL + anon key — public by design; RLS is what protects data
#   • Paystack PUBLIC key     — designed for client use
#   • Firebase client config   — public by design
#   • Google Maps key          — restrict it by app signature in GCP
#
# Anything that grants privilege or costs money per call is a SERVER secret
# and must never appear here. Those go in one of two places instead:
#
#   1. Supabase Edge Function secrets (Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets)
#      — for anything the backend needs at runtime.
#   2. `.env.tooling` (gitignored, NOT bundled) — for keys you only use from
#      your own machine for scripting/admin.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Bundled into the app (client-safe) ──────────────────────────────────

# Supabase — backend database, auth, storage
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Paystack — public key only. Safe to bundle (loaded via EnvConfig).
PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Firebase — push notifications / analytics
FIREBASE_API_KEY=
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=

# Google Maps — rider tracking, delivery routing, campus maps
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ── NOT in this file — Supabase Edge Function secrets ───────────────────
#
# Set these in Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets. The Flutter client
# never sees them.
#
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY  — used by verify-paystack-payment
#   TERMII_API_KEY       — used by phone-otp (sending/verifying SMS OTPs
#                          moved server-side; the client no longer holds
#                          this key, because it is billable per message)

# ── NOT in this file — .env.tooling (your machine only) ─────────────────
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — bypasses all RLS. Admin scripting only.
